  "title": {
    "text": "More rural regions have less job churn",
    "subtitle": [
      "ITL2 regions: share of residents in rural areas (Census) against job reallocation rate pooled 2018\u201324. Correlation -0.66; -0.68 for England and Wales only.",
      "Rural is defined differently in each nation: settlements under 10,000 people in England and Wales (2021), under 3,000 in Scotland (2022), under 5,000 in NI (2011),",
      "so Scottish shares are understated relative to the rest of the UK. Grey line = fit across all regions. London has no rural areas.",
      "Sources: ONS Longitudinal Business Database (Secure Access, SN 9501); ONS, NRS and NISRA population estimates; authors' calculations."
    ]
  },
